  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PHL 801 supports the Employers Confederation of the Philippines (ECOP) in strengthening its institutional capacity to become more member-driven and service-oriented. Expectations on businesses in terms of their environmental, social and governance (ESG) footprints have increased considerably in recent years. The intervention will support the development of ECOP&#x2019;s ESG programme which will designed to help enterprises navigate this emerging complex environment. This initiative builds on ECOP&#x2019;s existing Responsible Business Conduct programme and is introducing a range of ESG-focused learning sessions and support services, including trainings, tools, and templates under each of the E,S,G pillars that aim to strengthen ESG adoption in enterprise operations. This new programme will also integrate ECOP&#x2019;s existing work on occupational safety and health, diversity, equity, and inclusion, industrial relations and social dialogue, due diligence, human resource development, and the Sustainable Development Goals. The suite of ECOP ESG tools will include the WeCheck gender self-assessment tool; the NaviGate an AI-powered compliance platform that will offer real-time advice on labour laws, OSH, ESG standards, DEI, the SDG Value Scan; and the LEADER ESG scan tool.  A new training programme will be launched also. ILO support aims to help ECOP improve relevant ECOP services, expand its membership. Beneficiaries include ECOP members, potential members and affiliated chapters across the country. The strategy is implemented in collaboration with national stakeholders and contributes to strengthening the voice and representation of employers in national development and social dialogue processes.</narrative>
  </description>
